WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:02.564
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.564 --> 00:00:05.473
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.473 --> 00:00:08.269
will solve all of the
worlds major problems.

00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:10.201
So to help you on your
journey, today's message

00:00:10.201 --> 00:00:13.610
is don't sleep walk through life.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.682
Over to you, Warren Buffett.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.744
(rooster croaks)

00:00:17.744 --> 00:00:22.369
♫ I wake up every morning,
espresso keep me going.

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:25.952
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:29.531
- I advise students, as much as possible,

00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:32.778
look for the job that you
would take if you didn't need

00:00:32.778 --> 00:00:35.406
a job, I mean don't
sleep walk through life.

00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:38.403
Don't say it's all going to be great.

00:00:38.403 --> 00:00:40.113
I'll do this and I'll do that.

00:00:40.113 --> 00:00:43.406
I'm just marking time
until I get to be older.

00:00:43.406 --> 00:00:45.041
I've told people that's like saving up sex

00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:48.193
for your old age.
(laughter)

00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:50.549
It is not a good idea.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.799
(laughter)

00:00:54.371 --> 00:00:56.621
(applause)

00:00:58.486 --> 00:01:00.846
- [Interviewer] What are
you urging them to do?

00:01:00.846 --> 00:01:04.986
- I'll explain just
what I'm talking about.

00:01:04.986 --> 00:01:07.236
(laughter)

00:01:09.687 --> 00:01:14.420
You really want to be
doing what you love doing.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.908
And you can't necessarily
find it on your first job.

00:01:16.908 --> 00:01:19.600
But don't give up before you find it.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.075
- One of the best questions
that you could ask yourself,

00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:24.021
period, is if I had all of the money

00:01:24.021 --> 00:01:26.064
in the world, what would I do?

00:01:26.064 --> 00:01:28.013
Ask yourself, if you had all of the money

00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:30.297
in the world, what would you do?

00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:32.088
Because when you answer that question,

00:01:32.088 --> 00:01:35.924
it tells you what you should
actually be doing right now.

00:01:35.924 --> 00:01:37.607
Most people have no idea.

00:01:37.607 --> 00:01:39.228
Most people don't know
what they would be doing.

00:01:39.228 --> 00:01:41.218
And as a result, people
sleep walk through life.

00:01:41.218 --> 00:01:43.380
They're just trying to
their next mortgage payment

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.886
or their rent payment, or
just kind of scraping by.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:49.451
Constantly in survival
mode, sleep walking.

00:01:49.451 --> 00:01:51.380
Instead of actually
building something amazing.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.435
I had a recent meeting with
somebody who is on my team

00:01:53.435 --> 00:01:56.815
part time and I was asking her,
okay, I asked that question.

00:01:56.815 --> 00:01:59.183
If you had all of the money in
the world, what would you do?

00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:01.988
And she was talking about
going traveling and bringing

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.525
her parents to Canada and buying a house

00:02:04.525 --> 00:02:05.761
and all of these things.

00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:07.838
I said okay great, that's
done, that's taken care of.

00:02:07.838 --> 00:02:11.107
You traveled, you saw all of
the places you want to see.

00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:14.158
You brought your parents
over, you bought a house.

00:02:14.158 --> 00:02:17.509
You brought your whole family
over, great, all that's done.

00:02:17.509 --> 00:02:20.382
And you still have money,
what are you going to do?

00:02:20.382 --> 00:02:23.727
I don't know, and that's the problem.

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.510
That's the work that you should be doing.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.205
That's the work that if you start doing,

00:02:27.205 --> 00:02:29.412
it's going to be able to
give you the money to afford

00:02:29.412 --> 00:02:32.303
all of these things that
you want to do in your life.

00:02:32.303 --> 00:02:35.216
But as long as your
working for somebody else.

00:02:35.216 --> 00:02:38.300
Not chasing your dreams, not
sure of what you want to do.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.268
Not having a plan and just sleep walking.

00:02:41.268 --> 00:02:43.562
Then those financial things
that you have in mind are never

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.980
going to come true,
you're always going to be

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.645
in survival mode and so it's a
good question to ask yourself

00:02:49.645 --> 00:02:51.087
at least once a quarter.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:53.720
If you had all of the money in the world,

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.360
what would you do with it?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.898
Because our first instinct
is all of the money things,

00:02:57.898 --> 00:03:00.293
all of the things that we
feel that we're missing.

00:03:00.293 --> 00:03:02.574
Like the vacation, like
the car, like the house,

00:03:02.574 --> 00:03:04.541
like the bills, all of that stuff.

00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:06.945
But you still have money
left over, what would you

00:03:06.945 --> 00:03:08.945
be doing with your life?

00:03:09.881 --> 00:03:12.547
And until you get a really
solid answer then you're never

00:03:12.547 --> 00:03:15.390
really going to have a great
plan for where you're going,

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.928
in your life and in your business.

00:03:16.928 --> 00:03:18.732
If I had all of the money in the world,

00:03:18.732 --> 00:03:19.911
I'd be helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:19.911 --> 00:03:21.252
I'd be doing what I'm doing.

00:03:21.252 --> 00:03:23.915
I would still be making YouTube videos.

00:03:23.915 --> 00:03:27.822
I designed my life in such
a way that I haven't had

00:03:27.822 --> 00:03:31.661
to make a decision based
totally off of money

00:03:31.661 --> 00:03:33.336
for a very, very long time.

00:03:33.336 --> 00:03:36.137
I don't take on a great deal
that I don't want to work with.

00:03:36.137 --> 00:03:39.491
I don't make YouTube videos
only trying to make money.

00:03:39.491 --> 00:03:41.534
Right, I don't do anything
in my life, in my business

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:44.081
just trying to take a cash trap.

00:03:44.081 --> 00:03:45.702
And I think it's important.

00:03:45.702 --> 00:03:47.293
I think it's important
that when you deep down

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.473
understand that this is the
work that you would be doing

00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:53.783
regardless of if you've got
pay check for it or not.

00:03:53.783 --> 00:03:56.007
If you look at every single
successful entrepreneur

00:03:56.007 --> 00:03:58.657
and what drives them, what motivates them,

00:03:58.657 --> 00:04:01.307
it's never money, money is
important but it's never

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.382
the number one and so I
would strongly encourage you

00:04:04.382 --> 00:04:07.749
to ask yourself, at least once a quarter,

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:10.017
if you had all of the money in the world,

00:04:10.017 --> 00:04:13.664
what would you be doing
in your day to day life?

00:04:13.664 --> 00:04:16.321
And then go out and find
a way to start doing that

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:19.391
right now, it doesn't have
to be some big pipe dream,

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:21.895
it doesn't have to be only
when you win the lottery

00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:23.997
or when you sell your business, right now.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.622
Find a small way to get started right now.

00:04:26.622 --> 00:04:28.938
Because it's possible
and that's how you stop

00:04:28.938 --> 00:04:31.271
sleep walking through life.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.259
So the question of the day today is,

00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:34.359
I want you to answer
that question right now.

00:04:34.359 --> 00:04:35.691
If you had all of the money in the world,

00:04:35.691 --> 00:04:38.220
what would you be doing with it?

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.774
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:39.774 --> 00:04:41.015
I'm really curious to find out.

00:04:41.015 --> 00:04:43.418
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Antonio Centeno

00:04:43.418 --> 00:04:46.401
from Real Men Real Style,
Antonia thank you so much

00:04:46.401 --> 00:04:48.954
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.882
and posting it to your Twitter account.

00:04:50.882 --> 00:04:53.133
I really appreciate the
support man and I'm so glad

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.996
that you're enjoying the read.

00:04:54.996 --> 00:04:56.732
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:04:56.732 --> 00:04:59.228
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:04:59.228 --> 00:05:02.252
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:05:02.252 --> 00:05:03.985
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:03.985 --> 00:05:06.956
for a nother shot of espresso.

00:05:06.956 --> 00:05:11.123
♫ I wake up every morning,
espresso keep me going.

00:05:15.575 --> 00:05:17.700
- The type of person
you are kind of points

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.048
to the things that you're good at.

00:05:19.048 --> 00:05:20.625
Are you 12, you're not going to know.

00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:22.652
Are you 16, you're not going to know.

00:05:22.652 --> 00:05:26.706
If you're 18, maybe if you
have a special talent, right.

00:05:26.706 --> 00:05:28.898
You know, you can throw a
baseball a 100 miles an hour.

00:05:28.898 --> 00:05:31.432
You can sing and your voice
is incredible, you know.

00:05:31.432 --> 00:05:34.493
You're a concert pianist,
you're a chess grand master.

00:05:34.493 --> 00:05:36.680
If you have a specific skill set or talent

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.691
that just immediately
propels you to the top,

00:05:38.691 --> 00:05:40.299
yeah, you want to follow that.

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:42.517
But I remember having a
list, I still have it.

00:05:42.517 --> 00:05:44.700
When I graduated from
college, I was getting ready

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.996
to graduate and all of
the different industries

00:05:46.996 --> 00:05:49.239
that I thought I might want to partake in.

00:05:49.239 --> 00:05:52.370
When you find something
you're good at, go for it.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.333
I was never really in to
technology when I was a kid

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:57.890
but then as I got a job
that used it, I found out

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:01.100
I was good at it and once I
found out I was good at it,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.911
then it became a lot more fun.

00:06:02.911 --> 00:06:03.744
You know when you're good at something,

00:06:03.744 --> 00:06:05.364
it's almost always fun.

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:08.030
And once it was fun and
I combined that with my

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.994
business skills then I saw,
okay I know how to make money

00:06:10.994 --> 00:06:12.797
with this stuff because
I know how to sell.

00:06:12.797 --> 00:06:15.394
Now I know tech, that gives
me something I love to do

00:06:15.394 --> 00:06:18.464
and so when I tell people
the key is find something

00:06:18.464 --> 00:06:20.451
you love to do and be great at it.

00:06:20.451 --> 00:06:22.697
- If you're passionate
and you're successful,

00:06:22.697 --> 00:06:25.030
you'll wake up one day rich.

00:06:26.061 --> 00:06:27.896
You won't really be going for the cash,

00:06:27.896 --> 00:06:29.210
it will just happen to you.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:32.007
Everybody I talk to that's had success,

00:06:32.007 --> 00:06:35.659
doesn't remember the day
they became a millionaire.

00:06:35.659 --> 00:06:38.242
No idea, not important to them.

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:41.514
They remember winning,
they remember building

00:06:41.514 --> 00:06:44.181
a business and being successful.

00:06:45.227 --> 00:06:49.885
Again, the pursuit of freedom
manifests itself in passion.

00:06:49.885 --> 00:06:51.983
That's really what it's about.

00:06:51.983 --> 00:06:56.015
- I do not make any decisions
based on money, none.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.692
It's the worst way to make
a decision, which I know

00:06:58.692 --> 00:07:02.503
is so hard to say, I mean I
didn't grow up with any money.

00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:07.390
And I know so many of us, our
families have a lot at stake.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:12.276
They put a lot into us, made
a lot of sacrifices for us.

00:07:12.276 --> 00:07:15.366
And you say you don't have
the luxury of doing that,

00:07:15.366 --> 00:07:17.716
but I actually think you do.

00:07:17.716 --> 00:07:21.136
You will be more successful if
you make decisions based upn

00:07:21.136 --> 00:07:25.235
what is going to feed your
soul, make you feel value,

00:07:25.235 --> 00:07:30.114
valued, validated, have you
waking up in the morning

00:07:30.114 --> 00:07:32.525
and racing to work, whatever it might be.

00:07:32.525 --> 00:07:34.586
And I can tell you, after
a short amount of time,

00:07:34.586 --> 00:07:36.949
money will not be enough.

00:07:36.949 --> 00:07:39.767
At the end of the day, a
bigger pay check is another

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:43.467
suit or more real estate,
more square footage.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.343
That's what it comes down to.

00:07:45.343 --> 00:07:49.343
You end up with another
room and a fuller closet

00:07:51.009 --> 00:07:54.565
and after a while, that's
not going to do it.

